Description: Refresh test oracles for the pinned GIS stack on noble
 PROJ 9.8 reports the missing CRS identifier. GEOS 3.14.1 changes the
 predicates for the invalid zero-length lines in relations7/8; the expected
 values were checked directly against all eight GEOS C API functions.
 SQLite 3.45 renders huge integral doubles differently at precision zero
 and precision fifteen. Accept only identical finite binary64 values for
 the 100+ digit coordinate tokens in buffer-overflow tests; retain exact
 byte comparison for all other content and retain the original 1e128
 inputs, 16 KiB strings and excessive requested precision.
 This changes tests only, not production library behavior.
Author: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-04

